@startuml
title P1 Telegram Media Flow - Legacy Default vs Inline Routing

actor "Telegram User" as User
participant "Telegram Transport" as Bot
participant "SubmitMedia" as Submit
participant "History Model" as History
participant "Presentation Model" as Labels
participant "Transmission Service" as Tx
participant "Presence Surface" as Presence
participant "App / Bot Read Views" as Views

User -> Bot : send voice, audio or document hint
Bot -> Submit : submit(source=telegram)
Submit -> History : media status = processing
Submit --> Bot : media ready or error

alt media failed, unsupported group or Phase-2-only attachment
  Bot -> Labels : map honest failure text
  Labels --> User : unsupported / too long / track path deferred
else media ready
  Bot -> Labels : render delivery + audience labels
  Labels --> User : inline actions\noverlay / interrupt / after_current

  alt user takes no action
    Bot -> Tx : legacy default after_current\npersonal/broadcast defaults
    note right of Tx
      Acceptance ordering stays by
      coordinator acceptance time.
    end note
  else user taps inline action
    User -> Bot : callback(delivery, audience)
    Bot -> Tx : CreateTransmission(...)
  end

  Tx -> History : accepted / preparing / playing / played / partial / error
  Tx -> Presence : DND/block/capability result
  History -> Labels : sender + target + receipt labels
  Presence -> Labels : current approach + availability labels
  Labels --> Views : same wording for app and bot
end

note bottom
  Pairwise approach remains the Phase 1 shared-air shape.
  Track queue/replace and offline inbox stay deferred to Phase 2.
end note

@enduml
